      <div type="clause" n="71.4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 71.4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71.4" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif he to þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> cingce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.17-2"/> furðor cyððe hæbbe: II<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.11"/> hors, I<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.18-2"/> gesadelod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.19-2"/> ⁊ oðer unsadelod, ⁊ swurd ⁊ II<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.11"/> spera ⁊ II<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.11"/> scyldas ⁊ L<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.20-2"/> mances goldes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71.4" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf he to ðam kyncge furðor cyððe hæbbe: II hors, an gesadelod ⁊ oðer ungesadolod ⁊ an swyrd ⁊ II spera ⁊ twegen scyldas ⁊ fiftig mancus goldes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71.4" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif he to þam cyninge forþor cyððe hæbbe: II hors, an gesadelod ⁊ oðer ungesadelod ⁊ I swurd ⁊ twa spera ⁊ II scyldas ⁊ fiftig mancos goldes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71.4" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si notus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.14"/> sit regi: II<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.15"/> equi — unus cum sella<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.16"/>, alius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.17"/> sine sella<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.18"/> — et I gladius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.19"/> et II lanceę et totidem scuta et L manc.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.20"/> auri.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71.4" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>et, si notus fuerit regi: duos equos, unus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.7"/> cum sella et alius sine, gladium unum et duas lanceas et duo scuta et quinquaginta mancas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.2"/> auri;</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71.4" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi apud regem maiorem familiaritatem habeat: duo equi, unus cum sella et alter sine sella, unus gladius et due lancee et duo scuta et L mance auri.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="71a.4" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="210" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ gyf he to ðam kyncge furðor cyððe hæbbe—II hors, an gesadelod ⁊ oðer ungesadolod, ⁊ an swyrd ⁊ II spera ⁊ twegen scyldas ⁊ fiftig mancus goldes.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="290" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gif he to þam cingce furðor cyððe hæbbe: II hors, I gesadelod and oðer unsadelod, and swurd and II spera and II scyldas and L mances goldes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn er zum König weitergehende Beziehung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_71-4.lnote.de.1"/> hat: 2 Pferde, 1 gesattelt und das andere ungesattelt, und 1 Schwert und 2 Lanzen und 2 Schilde und 50 Mancus Gold.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if he has a closer relationship to the king: 2 horses, 1 saddled and the other unsaddled, and 1 sword and 2 spears and 2 shields and 50 mancuses of gold.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="211" ed="#robertson"/>And if he stands in a more intimate relationship to the king<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_71-4.robnote.n.1"/>, it shall be two horses, one saddled and the other unsaddled, and one sword and two spears and two shields and 50 mancuses of gold.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="472" ed="#whitelock"/>And if he has a more intimate relation with the king: two horses, one saddled and one unsaddled, and a sword and two spears and two shields and 50 mancuses of gold.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="291" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if he has a closer relationship with the king: two horses, one saddled and the other unsaddled, and a sword, two spears, two shields, and fifty mancuses of gold.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 359, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">apud regem promotiorem iustitiam habeat <hi rend="italic">Hn</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">apud regem promotiorem iustitiam habeat Hn</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e. duo <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e. duo Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ssella <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ssella Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a. s. s. <hi rend="italic">zweimal K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a. s. s. twice K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lis <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lis Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dium <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dium Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mancas <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> mance <hi rend="italic">RTHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mancas K; mance RTHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.17-2" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyningc forþor. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyningc forþor. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">twa <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">twa Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.18-2" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">án <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">án Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.19-2" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-de ⁊ o. ungesadolode ⁊ I s. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-de ⁊ o. ungesadolode ⁊ I s. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.20-2" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fiftig mancos <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fiftig mancos Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cum s. unum, al. <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cum s. unum, al. Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">marcas <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">marcas Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_71-4.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Intime Freundschaft’ (<hi rend="italic">s</hi>. Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl. s. v. cyððu</hi>) mit dem König bezeichnet den höheren Rang im Gefolge; Brunner I² 193</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Intimate friendship’ (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl. s. v. cyððu</hi>) with the king denotes the higher rank in the retinue; Brunner I² 193</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_71-4.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Lit. ‘if he has relations with the king to a higher degree (than others).’ <hi rend="italic">furðor</hi> here is an adverb.</seg></note>
